<tr valign="top" height="50" >
<td tEditID="c1r1" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; color:#000000; bEditID:r3st1; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r1" locked="1" >
<![CDATA[<font face="arial">{!Contact.FirstName},</font>]]></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" height="300" >
<td tEditID="c1r2" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; color:#000000; bEditID:r3st1; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r2" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[<p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">Thank you for your
interest in the </span><a href="https://webapp4.asu.edu/programs/t5/majorinfo/ASU00/ECHNUTMS/graduate/false?init=false&amp;nopassive=true"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:
&quot;Times New Roman&quot;">Master of Science in Human Nutrition</span></a><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"> at Arizona State University! I look forward to
assisting you as you consider your options at ASU.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><b><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">About the Program</span></b><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><span lang="EN" style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">The primary objective of the graduate program in Human Nutrition is to provide advanced training in the research methodologies and biochemical laboratory skills that are relevant to nutrition. Graduate students are expected to develop competencies in research methods and in advanced practice knowledge relevant to their area of study. The skills and knowledge acquired during the course of training should enable each student to develop professional competencies that can be applied to significant problems and issues within the field of nutrition and dietetics.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><span lang="EN" style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><span lang="EN" style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">The
MS degree is aimed at two categories of students:<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><span lang="EN" style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">&nbsp;</span></p><ol style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-top: 0in;" start="1" type="1">
 <li class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><b><span lang="EN" style="font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;
     mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN">Students
     who want to become Registered Dietitians with the MS degree:</span></b><span lang="EN" style="font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;
     mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN"><br>
     The majority of applicants in teh ASU MS in Human Nutrition program plan on completing the combined two-year MS degree, plus Dietetic Internship (DI) before taking the RD exam. Only students who have completed an accredited Didactic Program in Dietetics (DPD) are eligible for the combined MS/DI option.<o:p></o:p></span></li>
</ol><div style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span><font face="Arial, sans-serif">Applications to the ASU MS/DI program for fall only have a deadilne of <span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span>February 15.</font></div><div style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><br></font></div><div style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span>Applications to the ASU/VA MS/DI program for spring only have a <span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span>deadline of September 25.&nbsp;</font></div><div style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><br></font></div><p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><span lang="EN" style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">Learn
more about the MS in Human Nutrition with optional </span><a href="https://snhp.asu.edu/programs/internships/dietetic-internship"><span lang="EN" style="font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:
&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN">Dietetic Internship</span></a><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><span lang="EN" style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">&nbsp;</span></p><ol style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-top: 0in;" start="2" type="1">
 <li class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><b><span lang="EN" style="font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;
     mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN">Students
     who want to complete an MS degree in Nutrition only, without the RD
     credential:</span></b><span lang="EN" style="font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
     &quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-ansi-language:
     EN"><br>
     Less than 10% of students who wish to complete this MS degree without the
     dietetic internship are admitted each year – usually in order to go on to
     a PhD program or apply to medical school. It is highly recommended that studetns have undergraduate degrees in nutrition or science to be a competitive applicant. Students can complete only the MS degree without the dietetic internship in approximately one year depending upon successful completion of their research thesis.</span></li></ol><div style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span>The priority application deadline is February 15; however, applications&nbsp;</font></div><div style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span>will be considered for fall admission until June 15 on a space available <span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span>basis.&nbsp;</font></div><div style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><br></font></div><p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><b><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">About Admission</span></b><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">We seek applicants with
strong GRE scores on all portions of the exam. However, there are no minimum
scores for the GRE examination, which is evaluated in the context of your
entire application package. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">International student information is found on the <a href="https://students.asu.edu/graduate/international">Graduate Admissions</a> webpage. &nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"><br></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"><a href="https://students.asu.edu/tuitionandfees">Tuition and fee information</a> can be calculated according to your residency and degree program.&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">Please let me know if
you have any questions and thank you so much for your interest!<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">Regards,<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><b><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">Amanda Kling, MEd</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"><o:p></o:p></span></b></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">Graduate Program and Dietetic Internship Administrative Coordinator<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: arial; margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><font color="#990000"><b><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">School of Nutrition and
Health Promotion,&nbsp;</span><span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;">College of Health Solutions</span></b></font></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">550 North 3rd Street I
Phoenix, AZ 85004 I MC 3020<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;">Office: 602.496.0869 I
Fax: 602.496.1873 I </span><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><a href="mailto:amanda.kling@asu.edu">Amanda.Kling@asu.edu</a></font></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;">





















































</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: arial; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>]]></td>
</tr>
